Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-10-2001||08:21 AM||||I looked at my rad yesterday when I was putting my headlight motors back on, the thin rad metal(metal thats like an acordian) is crumbling.. The rad dont leak.. Anyone have this happen before?  Should I get it recored before it does bust on me? Or is there a good chance it will never harm anything?<P>Thanks<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-10-2001||11:21 AM||||Those fins disapate the heat from the radiator.I dont know how bad your deterioration is .But if it is not leaking and or over heating.I would just keep an eye on it,and not change it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||08-10-2001||12:19 PM||||acid rain? better keep an eye on it. it will eventully corrode thru.||||reg||1
Z||000003||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-10-2001||12:26 PM||||about the middle of the radiator (top to bottom) there are about 3 fins on the drivers side thats worn out.. they only go halfway across the rad.<P> Thanks for the info!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||SteveJ||08-10-2001||03:27 PM||||Those fins keep the tubes from bending. As you go through repeated heating cycles the tubes will soon flex themselves into failure.||||reg||1
Z||000005||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-10-2001||04:46 PM||||ouch..  thanks for the warnings..  <P>can a rad shop replace just the fins without recorring the whole rad?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||08-10-2001||06:11 PM||||no, tubes and cooling fins are all manufactured together and called the radiator core. have to replace it. ThinK Fiero Store sells new core for $200. May get one like Modine locally for $150 or so, Its ez to replace. as long as its not leaking dont fool around with it, cause if its brittle youll make it leak.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||1
